      "writtenOn": "2020-12-17T08:52:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "ApexInfo (and ApexContents) currently don\u0027t hold paths. They just provide contextual information (like apex name, min sdk version, etc.) which previously was stored in a global variable, which was one of the major blockers to the bazel transition. \n\nHowever, in this CL, the struct is used as a means to pass the output paths to its \"dependencies\", so that they can use the output paths as inputs. In doing so, the output paths are constructed in a mutator (not in GenerateAndroidBuildActions), at a non-standard place (out/soong/.intermediates/.../\u003cmodulename\u003e/\u003carch\u003e/), both of which look quite new to me.\n\nI really want to hear opinion from the Soong team.",
      "parentUuid": "2f4e7297_9bf686ec",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 215,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 230,
        "endChar": 2
      },
